+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` checks `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse`, so the model can read it and correct the call within the tool-round bound; only an unknown tool name throws.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Input missing a required property is rejected with a result that names the property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a result naming it, without running the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L28)).
+- Valid input carrying an unlisted extra property reaches the executor unchanged, exactly once, and invalid input never does ([validated by: passes valid input with an unlisted extra property to the executor unchanged, exactly once, and not invalid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L38)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected naming its path and expected type, and the message never contains the offending value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming its path and expected type, never the offending value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+- A schema that cannot be compiled makes `register` throw, and the message names the tool ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema current at that call, not a stale cached one ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L70)).
+- A rejected payload leaves no property value in any log line or returned text ([validated by: writes no log line containing a rejected payload value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L93)).
